              "type": "Type"
            }
          ],
          "content": "Rembrandt’s rapid progress as a printmaker is easy to see in this group of poor wretches. The seated woman is still somewhat crudely executed, but the beggar woman with a gourd and her male companion already testify to greater mastery of the technique. The little prints of a man and a woman are etched in the finer style that Rembrandt was to develop later."
        },
        {
          "type": "LinguisticObject",
          "classified_as": [
